{"repositoryId":268385172,"availability":"available","full":"remram44/twitch-vod-sync","name":"twitch-vod-sync","description":"Watch multiple Twitch VOD in sync. Useful for competitions","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":15,"forks":7,"created":"2020-05-31T23:57:32Z","updated":"2026-02-14T03:54:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://remram44.github.io/twitch-vod-sync/","topics":["hacktoberfest","react","static-web-app","twitch","video","video-player","video-streaming","webapp"],"demo":"https://remram44.github.io/twitch-vod-sync/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.479Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.479Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.479Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.479Z","stars":15,"forks":7}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a web application that can show multiple recorded videos from Twitch, syncing them exactly.","If you want to see the streams of multiple people playing together, applications like MultiTwitch.tv (GitHub) or Twitch's own \"Squad Stream\" mode can help. However if you are watching the streams after the fact (or after the event) or if the streams are not exactly synced (because they use different delays, common in competitions) it won't work.","This application can bring up multiple VOD (recorded streams), obtain their starting date from the API, and show them in perfect sync. You will still need to input the appropriate delay for each stream if different."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/remram44/twitch-vod-sync/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"8884aedb396bf264076022e648071be5dd064122387e28e676f34d42bee6a5e5","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.694Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:32:53.694Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a web application that can show multiple recorded videos from Twitch, syncing them exactly.","sourceUrl":"https://githu